From a9d8cdbfe95002c69e7094a37a9ca20df0f03f29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rayyan <rayyanwas02@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:18:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Append-only KV history, precision provenance, and the Phase 1
 gate

The token backends re-rendered the whole conversation each turn and kept the
longest common prefix with the cache. The harness rewrites assistant text
(strip, inserted newline) and chat templates such as Qwen3's drop the empty
think block from history, so the previous assistant message diverged and was
re-prefilled at READ precision. That recomputed tool-call KV at the wrong
bits and billed those tokens as READ cost, which would have contaminated the
READ-sensitivity estimates in the Phase 2 atlas.

- TokenBackend keeps generated tokens verbatim and appends only the chat
  template's tail (found by rendering with a sentinel assistant message)
- cached_bits records the precision of every cached token; restore re-feeds
  missing tokens at their original precision
- replay restores a backend snapshot taken before each turn's observation
  instead of truncating by re-rendering
- reference trajectories in the atlas now keep their text
- scripts/phase1_gate.py: format, reliability, low-bit signal, cache and
  atlas-cost checks with an atlas wall-clock estimate
- docs/PHASE1_RUNBOOK.md and a gate cell in the Colab notebook
- tests: provenance invariant, exact template tail, restore fast-forward,
  gate loop on the token backend (38 tests)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
