-  Before each sample the backend cache is cut back to before the last observation, so the READ
-  segment is always re-prefilled at the intended precision.
+  Each sample restores a backend snapshot taken before that turn's observation was
+  prefilled; `restore` re-feeds any missing tokens at their original precision, so the READ
+  segment is re-prefilled at the probe precision and everything before it is unchanged.
 - **Phase hinter.** Policies see whether the next call will end the episode through a
   deployable hinter that uses only the agent's own observations, never the oracle.
   `OraclePhasePolicy` (P3) gets the true phase and is an upper bound only.
